*   **The $H^+$ and $OH^-$ Jump Mechanism:** Conductance of $H^+$ and $OH^-$ is exceptionally high because they don't just "travel"; they "jump" through the hydrogen-bonded water network (Grotthuss mechanism), making them faster than any other ion.
