### 3. ALL IMPORTANT FORMULAS

| Formula | Context | Meaning of Variables |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **$\Lambda^\circ_m = x\lambda^\circ_+ + y\lambda^\circ_-$** | Kohlrausch's Law | $x, y$: Stoichiometric coefficients of ions. |
| **$\alpha = \Lambda_m / \Lambda^\circ_m$** | Weak Electrolytes | $\alpha$: Degree of dissociation. |
| **$K = \frac{C \Lambda_m^2}{\Lambda^\circ_m (\Lambda^\circ_m - \Lambda_m)}$** | Dissociation Constant | Derived by substituting $\alpha$ into $K = C\alpha^2/(1-\alpha)$. |
| **$S = \frac{\kappa \times 1000}{\Lambda^\circ_m}$** | Solubility | $S$: Solubility in mol/L; $\kappa$: Specific conductance. |

